I've never been as thankful for unholy water as I was in a recent game
where, for the first time ever, I reached the Planes quickly enough not
to have forgotten any spells, which I usually depend on to help locate
the portals.  Fortunately I was carrying some unholy water and a spare
unicorn horn, which when cursed was an acceptable substitute.

Went on to ascend my first Archaeologist that time.  I started my first
Healer game soon after (one of the only two roles left I haven't
ascended).  It was going really well, until I absentmindedly noshed on a
vanquished monster too soon after turning a boulder into a huge chunk of
meat and devouring it, and instantly choked to death.  I don't think
I've ever cast "stone to flesh" before, in any game, so I didn't have
the necessary caution burned into my synapses like I do with other
crucial bits of Nethack lore (like how to behave around cockatrices).  I
sure as hell do now, though.


